* **{c=red:Note:}** If you did not already do so, speak with {p:Cid} (in {p:Bastok} - {z:Metalworks} - Home Point #1) to begin this Mission.
* Talk to {n:Despachiaire} at the {z:Tavnazian Safehold} Home Point #3 - Top Floor (K-10).
** You may need to speak with him multiple times as he offers more than one cutscene at this point.

=4 Southern Legend
* Speak with {p:Perih Vashai} at (K-7) in {z:Windurst Woods} Home Point #1.

=4 Partners Without Fame
* Travel to (H-11) on {p:Purgonorgo Isle|Bibiki Bay - Purgonorgo Isle} in {p:Bibiki Bay} and speak with the {p:??? Warmachine} for a cutscene
** You can reach {p:Purgonorgo Isle} by taking the {z:Manaclipper} in {p:Bibiki Bay} (H-7).
*** You can use {p:Unity Warp} (Level 119) to bring you close to the Manaclipper dock.
*** Speak with {n:Fheli Lapatzuo} on the dock to make sure you're going to the right island **and** ensure that you have tickets from {n:Tswe Panipahr} nearby.
** Alternatively, you can clear the first 4 {p:Voidwatch} NMs on the {q:Tavnazian|VW Op. 026: Tavnazian Terrors|Tavnazian} path to gain a direct warp to the island, without having to have been there before. (recommended as you will be coming back later)
*** **Note:** This may be difficult for new players. Use x5 {i:Phase Displacers|Phase Displacer|3853} to weaken the NM. See the {i:Phase Displacer|Phase Displacer|3853} page for details.
*** Speak with a {p:Atmacite Refiner} after completing the quest to teleport to {p:Purgonorgo Isle}.
** Teleportation items such as the {@i:Nexus Cape|11538} {i:Nexus Cape|Nexus Cape|11538} or {@i:Custom Top +1|11274} {p:HQ Swimsuit Tops|Category:Swimwear} which can teleport directly to {p:Bibiki Bay - Purgonorgo Isle} only allow you to teleport to zones you've already visited; you only need to visit {p:Bibiki Bay} to meet this requirement.

* **(Optional)**: Head to (E-5) in {z:Windurst Walls} and speak with {p:Yoran-Oran} for additional dialogue.

=4 A Century of Hardship
\**{c=red:Note:}** While in {z:Newton Movalpolos}, farm the {@i:Gold Key|1684} {i:Gold Key|Gold Key|1684} (**{p:U|Uncommon (10%)}** droprate) after you finish the BCNM, exiting to {z:Newton Movalpolos}. This will save you some time later.
* Travel to {z:Oldton Movalpolos} and zone in for a cutscene.
** The {z:Gusgen Mines} {p:Survival Guide} will bring you very close to the {z:Oldton|Oldton Movalpolos} entrance.
** The {z:Oldton Movalpolos} {p:Survival Guide} will also trigger the cutscene.
* The next step is the BC at {z:Mine Shaft #2716|Mine Shaft 2716} and there are several options to get to the BC entrance. Any of the following options work (pick up the home point if you do not already have it):
** 1) (Fastest) Take the {z:Newton Movalpolos} Home Point #1 (Places you right outside the Mine Shaft #2716).
** 2) (Fast) Trade a {@i:Snow Lily|1725} {i:Snow Lily|Snow Lily|1725} to {n:Tarnotik} at (K-10) in {z:Oldton Movalpolos} and he will warp you there.
*** The {i:Lily|Snow Lily|1725} can be purchased from the Auction House ({@g:Auction House} > Materials > Alchemy) or dropped from {m:Uleguerand Tiger} in {z:Uleguerand Range}.
*** Make sure you collect the Home Point and you can warp back, otherwise you will need 2 {i:Lilies|Snow Lily|1725}.
** 3) Gamble with {n:Twinkbrix} at (E-13) in {z:Oldton Movalpolos} by trading him Gil (1~10,000) until you win the {@k} {p:Shaft 2716 operating lever}, then pay him 2000 more Gil to warp you there.
*** On {p:Lightsday}, trading Twinkbrix a certain amount of gil will make him use not-{i:loaded dice|Goblin Die|568}, giving you the best odds as if you had traded 10,000, and also changes his dialogue.
** 4) The old fashioned (long) way of walking through {z:Newton Movalpolos} and operating the furnace hatches.
*** This requires at least 3 people.
*** (Alternative walk) You only need 1 {@i:Firesand|947} {i:Firesand|Firesand|947} if someone can tractor you up the east ledge in Oldton Movalpolos at (K-10), the person raising runs from the hp in Newton Movalpolos to exit 3.
*** You can get the {p:Proto-Waypoint} this way too if you started the quest {q:Researchers from the West|Researchers from the West|Researchers from the West}. Tractor up the south ledge, it is used in multiple {M:The Voracious Resurgence Missions|The Voracious Resurgence Missions|The Voracious Resurgence Missions}.
**** The Proto-Waypoint into Newton Movalpolos is also fastest way to get to the mobs that drop Gold Key.
* Before the battle is commenced, make sure to zone out into {z:Newton Movalpolos} and attune to the Home Point just outside after being teleported to {z:Mine Shaft #2716|Mine Shaft 2716} (you will need this later on, several times).

* After you have made your way to {z:Mine Shaft #2716|Mine Shaft 2716} rest up and go over strategies. When you are ready, click on the **Shaft Entrance** and enter the battlefield "**A Century of Hardship**".
** **Note**: Take caution not to enter an ENM instead of the Mission battlefield __A Century of Hardship__. You will need to return here again for this Mission and you must wait 5 days before obtaining another {@k} {p:Shaft 2716 operating lever}.
** Buffs will wear when you enter so make sure to buff while inside the battlefield.

__With the lifting of the level cap on this Battlefield, this battle is now relatively trivial in difficulty. The walkthrough below was written for a level cap of 60.__
[Boss Name
{m:Chekochuk} ({p:BLM}){br}{m:Trikotrak} ({p:RDM}){br}{m:Swipostik} ({p:THF}){br}{m:Movamuq} ({p:WHM}){br}{m:Bugbby} ({p:WAR})
>Abilities
* All of the Moblins and Bugbby can also use their respective job's 2 Hour Ability.

>Notes
* All of the Moblins can call {m:Bugbby} to their aid at anytime during the fight so whoever is kiting/tanking Bugbby should be prepared to pull hate back.
* {s:Sleep} is unreliable but {p:Silence} works well.
* Try to {p:Silence} the mages and pick them off one at a time.
* If you can't keep {p:Silence} on them all reliably, focus on Silencing the BLM first.
* If you manage to get them to {s:Sleep} and happen to be fighting the WHM, {p:Benediction} will wake the rest of them up.

